  {
   "id": "ko_l1_pronunciation",
   "type": "pronunciation",
   "title": "Batchim basics and sound linking",
   "lessons": [
    {
     "id": "ko_l1_pronunciation_1",
     "title": "Batchim basics and sound linking",
     "summary": "Final consonants reduce to seven sounds, and they slide onto a following vowel.",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "table",
       "head": [
        "Final letter(s)",
        "Sounds like",
        "Example"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "ㄱ ㅋ ㄲ",
         "[k]",
         "책 [chaek]"
        ],
        [
         "ㄴ",
         "[n]",
         "산 [san]"
        ],
        [
         "ㄷ ㅅ ㅆ ㅈ ㅊ ㅌ ㅎ",
         "[t]",
         "옷 [ot]"
        ],
        [
         "ㄹ",
         "[l]",
         "물 [mul]"
        ],
        [
         "ㅁ",
         "[m]",
         "밤 [bam]"
        ],
        [
         "ㅂ ㅍ",
         "[p]",
         "밥 [bap]"
        ],
        [
         "ㅇ",
         "[ng]",
         "강 [gang]"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Linking (연음): when a syllable with a final consonant is followed by one starting with ㅇ, the consonant moves across: 한국어 → [한구거], 음악 → [으막], 옷이 → [오시]."
      },
      {
       "type": "tip",
       "text": "Write it as spelled, say it as linked. Spelling stays the same."
      }
     ],
     "questions": [
      {
       "type": "pronounce",
       "audio": "한국어",
       "translation": "Korean language",
       "prompt": "Say it linked: [한구거]",
       "skill": "pronunciation",
       "id": "ko_l1_pronunciation_1_q1"
      },
      {
       "type": "pronounce",
       "audio": "음악",
       "translation": "music",
       "prompt": "Linked: [으막]",
       "skill": "pronunciation",
       "id": "ko_l1_pronunciation_1_q2"
      },
      {
       "type": "pronounce",
       "audio": "옷",
       "translation": "clothes",
       "prompt": "Final ㅅ sounds like [t]",
       "skill": "pronunciation",
       "id": "ko_l1_pronunciation_1_q3"
      },
      {
       "type": "mcq",
       "prompt": "„옷“ on its own is pronounced:",
       "options": [
        "ot",
        "os",
        "oj"
